      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Even though you prefer to manage it yourself, persistent or frequent burning sensations in your chest shouldn't be ignored, as they could potentially indicate acid reflux or another underlying condition. Taking frequent, high doses of antacids is not advisable, as it could lead to other issues like nutrient imbalances or kidney problems. It would be wise to seek medical advice, especially if symptoms persist or worsen. In the meantime, addressing possible dietary habits, such as not eating too close to bedtime or eating smaller meals, might provide relief. Remember, your health is paramount, and a professional assessment can prevent potential complications in the future.",
